$depth — MiDaS depth maps from images

SUMMARY
  Estimates per-pixel depth with MiDaS and outputs a classic ControlNet-style
  depth map (grayscale: bright = near, dark = far) for each input image.

SYNTAX
  $depth
  $depth(detect_resolution=512)

INPUT
  images[] — source photos or frames.

OUTPUT
  images[] — depth map PNGs (same count as input).

ARGUMENTS
  detect_resolution=512 — resize long side for detection (higher = finer detail).

SETUP
  models/depth/dpt_hybrid-midas-501f0c75.pt
  Download:
    uv run python tools/download_models.py --upstream-fallback
  .venvs/media with controlnet-aux + torch. GPU when CUDA is available.
  AH_DEPTH_GPU=0 forces CPU inference.
  AH_EMULATE_DEPTH=1 for stub PNG output without models.

EXAMPLE
  @depth_maps: $folder('refs') -> $depth(detect_resolution=768)
  @control: $file('photo.png') -> $depth() -> $save('depth')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
